{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 859 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "c6f6d2e4eb42e4282ff456e574fbcfc24d62c4b158206bde5ea867804b9daf53" :edb/db-before-t 858 :edb/db-after-t 859 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534171 50 #inst "2026-10-06T07:13:28.393Z" 13194139534171 true] [17592186083155 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280258 13194139534171 true] [17592186083155 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280262 13194139534171 true] [17592186083158 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280237 13194139534171 true] [17592186083158 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280244 13194139534171 true] [17592186083158 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280251 13194139534171 true] [17592186280237 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280238 13194139534171 true] [17592186280237 1089 "q-102940" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280237 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534171 true] [17592186280237 1100 "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=2{t}^{2}+3,\\,y=3{t}^{5}+{t}^{3},\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=1.$" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280237 1113 #uuid "7624a235-ab14-553b-803a-f56f725749db" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280237 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2}(5{t}^{2}+1).\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{3{t}^{2}(5{t}^{2}+1)}{4t}=\\frac{3t(5{t}^{2}+1)}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{3(1)(5(1)^{2}+1)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280238 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280239 13194139534171 true] [17592186280238 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280240 13194139534171 true] [17592186280238 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280241 13194139534171 true] [17592186280238 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280242 13194139534171 true] [17592186280238 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280243 13194139534171 true] [17592186280238 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534171 true] [17592186280238 1041 "selection" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280238 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280239 13194139534171 true] [17592186280238 1110 #uuid "f4ab19c6-acbb-5c20-a748-33e4d8506737" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280239 1034 "\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280239 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534171 true] [17592186280239 1111 #uuid "580202dd-3fea-5679-af87-c2bc9c132183" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280240 1034 "\\frac{11}{4}" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280240 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534171 true] [17592186280240 1111 #uuid "92d654cf-26ee-54fa-9c1e-ef823f34bec3" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280241 1034 "\\frac{11}{2}" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280241 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534171 true] [17592186280241 1111 #uuid "e7c57dc7-1f1a-5a6e-b1a2-16b6f0e563df" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280242 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280242 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534171 true] [17592186280242 1111 #uuid "53825d27-7c1f-5288-b7f6-b208c4a85b1d" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280243 1034 "\\frac{15}{4}" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280243 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534171 true] [17592186280243 1111 #uuid "8f9373b0-73fa-5a8e-8ec4-b45683795d8a" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280244 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280245 13194139534171 true] [17592186280244 1089 "q-15457" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280244 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534171 true] [17592186280244 1100 "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,y={cos}^{2}⁡(t),\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280244 1113 #uuid "a30e060e-8fbc-5c7c-b8b0-45023960607a" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280244 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t).\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =-\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280245 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280246 13194139534171 true] [17592186280245 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280247 13194139534171 true] [17592186280245 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280248 13194139534171 true] [17592186280245 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280249 13194139534171 true] [17592186280245 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280250 13194139534171 true] [17592186280245 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534171 true] [17592186280245 1041 "selection" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280245 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280250 13194139534171 true] [17592186280245 1110 #uuid "bc35beed-7ff2-518c-977d-441db5683bef" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280246 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280246 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534171 true] [17592186280246 1111 #uuid "6ce6b55c-f51e-5a76-9782-ae5e346fb42e" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280247 1034 "-\\,\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280247 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534171 true] [17592186280247 1111 #uuid "b29d8346-6d37-530f-8757-381236111818" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280248 1034 "\\sqrt{3}" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280248 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534171 true] [17592186280248 1111 #uuid "517d6982-f305-577e-87cc-be4e0e966542" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280249 1034 "-\\,\\sqrt{3}" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280249 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534171 true] [17592186280249 1111 #uuid "0d60e1b7-d80e-5ec8-b197-8f8e3e7976c7" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280250 1034 "-\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280250 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534171 true] [17592186280250 1111 #uuid "1324b2b8-e238-5bff-8f34-2b102dd2d6eb" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280251 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280252 13194139534171 true] [17592186280251 1089 "q-15469" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280251 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534171 true] [17592186280251 1100 "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=2{t}^{3}+1,\\,y={t}^{4}+2{t}^{2},\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=1.$" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280251 1113 #uuid "7f9e0331-ffe6-5489-b436-faf1f0bea590" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280251 1145 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=6{t}^{2},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=4t({t}^{2}+1).\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{4t({t}^{2}+1)}{6{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({t}^{2}+1)}{3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2((1)^{2}+1)}{3\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280252 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280253 13194139534171 true] [17592186280252 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280254 13194139534171 true] [17592186280252 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280255 13194139534171 true] [17592186280252 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280256 13194139534171 true] [17592186280252 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280257 13194139534171 true] [17592186280252 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534171 true] [17592186280252 1041 "selection" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280252 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280255 13194139534171 true] [17592186280252 1110 #uuid "c5a81521-a24f-5dd0-87f2-f8493118e35e" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280253 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534171 true] [17592186280253 1103 #edb/ref 17